{"id": "comment_f224a143dbfe4e559533209473455a2a", "issue_id": "ENG-2400", "author_id": "usr_175c0d7bc72ed244", "parent_id": null, "body": "Connected to **ENG-2438 — Live-Ops scheduler resilience** (July 2025 postmortem follow-ups, never built).

Players stuck with lives not regenerating is a player-facing symptom of the shared Live-Ops Event Engine scheduler: it's a single point of failure and lives regen runs on the same tick loop as event firing, so a scheduler stall halts both. The remediation was documented after the July 2025 outage but never built, and the failure recurred Nov–Dec 2025. Tracking the remediation in ENG-2438 so this isn't floating unattached. Owners of the fix: Douglas + Arthur.
